WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.033
Hello everyone. I am Steve Kaufmann.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:09.032
Today is a special video. 

00:00:09.032 --> 00:00:13.031
It's not the normal learn languages subject, 

00:00:13.031 --> 00:00:24.029
instead I'm going to tell you how I’m preparing to make a special video introducing my channel. 

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:29.028
If you're interested in my channel, please subscribe.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:35.027
The thing is, if you're going to study languages, for sure you're going to make mistakes.

00:00:35.027 --> 00:00:38.026
It's not possible to not make mistakes.

00:00:38.026 --> 00:00:41.026
It's not possible that there won't be times when you don't understand.

00:00:41.026 --> 00:00:47.025
That's for certain. That's a predetermined condition of learning languages.

00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:52.024
So I thought that in order to make

00:00:52.024 --> 00:00:57.023
a trailer video to introduce my channel

00:00:57.023 --> 00:01:05.021
so I decided that I would try to use 20 different languages to record this video.

00:01:05.021 --> 00:01:09.020
The problem is it's not easy.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:14.019
Every time I try to record the video,

00:01:14.019 --> 00:01:21.018
every time I stop, I tend to move so the video isn't very good.

00:01:21.018 --> 00:01:27.017
So I tried to speak in those 20 languages in one go

00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:32.016
then of course I make mistakes.

00:01:32.016 --> 00:01:35.015
The result is I have a video like this.

00:01:35.015 --> 00:01:43.013
I’m getting get everyone to look at it. I would like to hear your opinions

00:01:43.013 --> 00:01:45.013
is it worth using or not?

00:01:45.013 --> 00:01:50.012
From one perspective the fact that there are mistakes is a good thing,

00:01:50.012 --> 00:01:55.011
because I really can't speak those 20 languages all very fluently.

00:01:55.011 --> 00:02:00.010
I speak some better than Chinese. Some are not at the same level as my Chinese.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:10.008
Some of them while visiting the country I was able to use them.

00:02:10.008 --> 00:02:18.006
Now it's not very easy for me I basically can't use them. If I want to recover my original level in that language,

00:02:18.006 --> 00:02:25.005
I would have to practice and practice a lot. I don't have the time because now I want to study Arabic.

00:02:25.005 --> 00:02:30.004
So the problem is right now you can look at this video

00:02:30.004 --> 00:02:35.003
there are lots of places, if you know the language, you will notice there are lots of errors.

00:02:35.003 --> 00:02:42.002
But should I show this video to let everyone see it and criticize?

00:02:42.002 --> 00:02:48.001
Language learning is like this. You can't have a perfect appearance.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:55.999
There will certainly be problems. Ok please have a look then let me know your opinion. Goodbye.

00:02:55.999 --> 00:03:02.031
Language learning for me is very important it's quite an important part of my life.

00:03:02.031 --> 00:03:12.029
Language learning is really not so difficult , what I think is important is the correct attitude.

00:03:12.029 --> 00:03:19.028
In order to learn languages you have to have a good attitude, and you have also to know that the world has changed. 

00:03:19.028 --> 00:03:27.026
There's so much content on the Internet, there's so much technology, like MP3 players and AirPods, which help us.

00:03:27.026 --> 00:03:35.025
Learning languages is a question of attitude. We have to enjoy the process of learning.

00:03:35.025 --> 00:03:47.022
When I learned Swedish I read a lot on the history of Sweden by Hermann Lindqvist

00:03:47.022 --> 00:04:01.019
But today there are so many things on the Internet and it's very important to read and listen a lot 

00:04:01.019 --> 00:04:06.018
and not to concentrate or worry too much about the details of grammar.

00:04:06.018 --> 00:04:12.017
When we learn languages we have to enjoy it. You have to find things that you feel are interesting.

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:18.016
It's very important that you have a reason to learn the language. 

00:04:18.016 --> 00:04:38.012
It can be the literature, the history, friends, or the family. It’s very important that you have this positive attitude to learn. 

00:04:38.012 --> 00:04:50.010
When I learned Italian I listened a lot, books like I Promessi Sposi. 

00:04:50.010 --> 00:05:05.007
For me it was very interesting although for Italians perhaps it isn't so because it's a subject at school 

00:05:05.007 --> 00:05:15.005
but for me and i'm going to make mistakes and making mistakes it's part of language learning

00:05:15.005 --> 00:05:25.003
Age is irrelevant. I started learning Russian when I was 60.

00:05:25.003 --> 00:05:39.033
Ukrainian, I learned Ukrainian because for me Ukrainian history was very interesting. 

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:48.032
Every language that I learn or have learned has brought me pleasure.

00:05:48.032 --> 00:06:02.029
Korean, when I learn Korean A long time ago, 

00:06:02.029 --> 00:06:10.027
there was no good content so it was difficult for me 

00:06:10.027 --> 00:06:23.025
but today at YouTube and Netflix there are lots of good Korean dramas.

00:06:23.025 --> 00:06:45.020
I studied Czech using wonderful programs from Czech radio, for example Toulky Ceskou Minolosti. 

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:53.019
I said the same for Polish but I have not yet been to Poland.

00:06:53.019 --> 00:07:08.016
I even studied Turkish for three months but I can't speak. One day I will.

00:07:08.016 --> 00:07:17.014
I learned Greek before visiting Crete and Athens.

00:07:17.014 --> 00:07:22.013
I learned Romanian before visiting the country.

00:07:22.013 --> 00:07:25.012
Why do I study Arabic? Arabic is difficult. 

00:07:25.012 --> 00:07:44.009
There are many  local dialects: Levantine, Egyptian, Gulf, North African, but the culture and history are very interesting.

00:07:44.009 --> 00:07:49.008
I may have forgotten a language or two.

00:07:49.008 --> 00:07:51.507
I certainly don't speak them all equally well.

00:07:51.507 --> 00:07:53.388
But every language that I have learned

00:07:53.388 --> 00:07:58.006
even to a limited degree has been a tremendous source of pleasure.

00:07:58.006 --> 00:08:01.005
And I think that we learn languages for our own reasons

00:08:01.005 --> 00:08:04.005
and for fun. And if we are willing to put in the time,

00:08:04.005 --> 00:08:09.004
and have a proper attitude and a good method we can all get there.

00:08:09.004 --> 00:08:14.003
And that's what I talk about at my channel so please subscribe and join me. 

